# Based on docs/planning_reference.md section 22, with two additions noted below.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# Test and type-checker caches (not in docs/planning_reference.md section 22, but these are
# generated by the pytest/hypothesis setup the image layer uses).
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# IDE
#
# .vscode/settings.json is shared deliberately (it pins the Python env manager
# for the team), so it is re-included below.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Temporary/generated media
output/
temp/
tmp/
*.tmp

# Logs
*.log

# Captured test-run output (pytest stdout redirected to a file so long runs can
# be inspected without flooding a terminal).
.pytest_out.txt

# Private keys
#
# docs/planning_reference.md section 22 suggests `keys/private/`, but the folder created by the
# project structure is `keys/demo_private/`, so both are listed.
#
# Deviation worth a team decision: section 22 also ignores `*.pem` and `*.key`
# outright, which would exclude PUBLIC keys as well. The receiver side of the
# A-to-B demo needs the public key, so `keys/public/` is explicitly re-included
# below. Private key material is still ignored everywhere else.
keys/private/
keys/demo_private/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Keep the committed folder placeholders and allow public keys to be shared.
!keys/**/.gitkeep
!keys/public/
!keys/public/*.pem

# evidence/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# An earlier version of this file excluded evidence/logs and evidence/results.
# That was wrong: docs/planning_reference.md section 5 lists evidence/screenshots, evidence/logs and
# evidence/results as project folders, and the assignment requires this material
# as submission evidence. Committing it is the point.
